==English==

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*(s)teg- (cover)}}
From {{der|en|la|detectus}}, perfect passive participle of {{m|la|detegere||to uncover or disclose}}, from {{m|la|de-}} + {{m|la|tegere||to cover}}; see {{m|en|tegument}}, {{m|en|tile}}, {{m|en|thatch}}.

Sense "to work or solve cases as a detective" a [[Appendix:Glossary#back-formation|back-formation]] from ''[[detective]]''.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/dɪˈtɛkt/|a=UK}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-detect.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɛkt|s=2}}

===Verb===
{{wikidata lexeme|L108}}
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[discover]] or [[notice]], especially by [[careful]] [[search]], [[examination]], or [[probe|probing]].
#: {{ux|en|The forensic examiners '''detected''' tiny traces of the poison on the suspect's gloves.}}
#: {{ux|en|On entering the room, I immediately '''detected''' the smell of gas.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive|informal}} To [[work]] or [[solve]] [[case]]s as a [[detective]].
#* {{quote-book|en|title=Hillary Waugh's Guide to Mysteries & Mystery Writing Novel|passage=In a detective story, a detective '''''detects'''''; an active effort is made to determine who committed a given crime, and detecting the identity of a criminal could not be done until there were detectives.|year=1991|author=w:Hillary Waugh|page=11|isbn=9780898794441|publisher={{w|Writer's Digest|Writer's Digest Books}}}}
#* {{RQ:en:New York Times|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20221217041126/https://www.nytimes.com/2019/05/09/movies/pokemon-detective-pikachu-review.html|passage= That aversion is tested when he teams up with Pikachu (voiced by Ryan Reynolds), his father's '''detecting''' partner, after the father appears to have been killed in an accident.|title='Pokémon Detective Pikachu' Review: A Cat and (Electric) Mouse Game|date=2019-05-09|author=Ben Kenigsberg}}

